ACT: README.md Quick Start step 4 (README.md:284-295).\nACCEPT: README states the entry count that the COMMITTED _index.json holds (or the file is regenerated in the same commit so the two agree), and the step is labelled as a write that dirties a tracked file, with the read-only alternative (`--validate`/`--tree`/`--impact`/`--graph`) named as the actual verification path.","ts":null,"complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-09-27T01:15:30.578947+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-16T19:15:00.000000+00:00","acceptance":"Two checks from repo root: (1) `python3 scripts/generate_index.py --generate --output /tmp/index-check.json` exits 0 and `python3 -c \"import json;a=json.load(open('/tmp/index-check.json'))['specs'];b=json.load(open('_index.json'))['specs'];print('OK' if a==b else 'FAIL')\"` prints OK, so regenerating leaves `git status --porcelain _index.json` empty (the documented step no longer dirties a tracked file); (2) `python3 -c \"import json,re;n=len(json.load(open('_index.json'))['specs']);m=[int(x) for x in re.findall(r'(\\d+) entries',open('README.md').read())];print('OK %d'%n if m and all(v==n for v in m) else 'FAIL %s'%m)\"` prints 'OK 464' \u2014 the Quick Start entry count matches the real index.","foreman_note":"Doc-severity re-triage 2026-11-03 (readme audit lane, tick speclang-readme-2026-11-03-15-46-12) per Bane ruling 2026-09-30: documentation findings are P4 (P5 for polish), never P1-P3. POLICY change only, not a new assessment \u2014 the finding is unchanged and still reproduces on the published tip 4cb5bbfb (README.md:287 '466 entries' vs committed _index.json).\n\n2026-11-16 tick 23-53: reset from in_progress \u2014 sibling wave worker for this row died without committing any code (worktree wt/* at base, no commits; main-tree diff absent for docs rows). Shared-checkout recovery by foreman tick speclang-foreman-2026-11-16-23-53-17: sibling wave SpecLang-dogfood-2026-11-16-22-47-48 workers were killed before committing. Worktree wt/<id> kept (some have par