 {"status":"complete","id":"README-16","title":"P4 \u2014 README install path omits the git-hook install step the suite needs: fresh clone npm test fails CI-005 'Hook not found' (1819 passed | 65 skipped vs README's 1826 | 58)","detail":{"fingerprint":"6979b3ec3f58f48122af208a8f6dd258fca330d5bd16af82bee89a48f9352952"},"priority":"P4","source":null,"reasoning":"README health sweep 2026-10-27 (readme audit lane). Doc severity P4 per Bane ruling 2026-09-30 (policy, not an assessment of the finding's class).\n\nFINDING (install-path): the README's \"From source\" install path (README.md:14-31: git clone -> npm install -> npm run build -> ./bin/speclang --help) is complete for running the CLI \u2014 verified this sweep \u2014 but it never installs the repo's git hooks, and the test suite depends on a hook that exists only in the maintainer's checkout. A stranger who follows the README verbatim and then runs the documented `npm test` (README.md:246, :388) gets a FAILING suite.\n\nMeasurements, same commands, two checkouts at the same commit:\n  A. maintainer checkout /home/kara/speclang:\n     $ npm test   ->  Test Files  97 passed | 4 skipped (101)\n                      Tests  1826 passed | 58 skipped (1884)\n     (identical with the host git config scrubbed: GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM=/dev/null)\n  B. stranger checkout: git clone --depth 1 file:///home/kara/speclang /var/tmp/speclang-fresh && npm install && npm run build\n     $ npm test   ->  Test Files  1 failed | 96 passed | 4 skipped (101)\n                      Tests  1819 passed | 65 skipped (1884)\n     failing file: tests/ci/ci005-precommit-hook.test.ts > \"CI-005: pre-commit hook hardening\"\n     $ npx vitest run tests/ci/ci005-precommit-hook.test.ts\n     Error: Hook not found: /var/tmp/speclang-fresh/.git/hooks/pre-commit\n      \u276f tests/ci/ci005-precommit-hook.test.ts:79:13\n         77|     const hookDst = join(scratch, \".git\", \"hooks\", \"pre-commit\");\n         78|     if (!existsSync(HOOK)) {\n         79|       throw new Error(`Hook not found: ${HOOK}`);\n     -> 7 tests skipped; Test Files 1 failed (1)\n     Same file in the maintainer checkout: Test Files 1 passed (1) | Tests 7 passed (7).\nMechanism: tests/ci/ci005-precommit-hook.test.ts:35 defines HOOK = join(REPO_ROOT, \".git\", \"hooks\", \"pre-commit\") and the suite throws when that file is absent. `.git/hooks/` is local, untracked state; the tracked hook the project actually ships is at .githooks/pre-commit (git ls-files .githooks/ -> .githooks/pre-commit, 827 bytes). The maintainer checkout has an untracked .git/hooks/pre-commit (2503 bytes) that no clone can have: `ls /var/tmp/speclang-fresh/.git/hooks/` lists only *.sample files.\nDocumentation gap, measured: `grep -rn 'hooksPath\\|githooks\\|install-hook\\|pre-commit' README.md GETTING-STARTED.md CONTRIBUTING.md PACKAGING.md package.json scripts/` -> no match. Nothing in the repo tells a contributor to run `git config core.hooksPath .githooks` (or copy the hook) \u2014 the missing step the suite silently requires.\nConsequence for the README's own claims: README.md:90, :451 and :534 state \"1826 passing | 58 skipped\" with no qualifier; that number is true only in a checkout that carries the untracked hook. The same clone measures 1819 | 65.\n\nRelated rows (cite, do not duplicate): README-2 owns the test-count claims (this row's measurement belongs in its fix); QA-SPECLANG-3 [pending P2] owns \"bare npm test on a fresh clone is red\" for the bin/speclang-spawn mechanism.\n\nFIX: (1) add the hook-install step to the README install path, e.g. `git config core.hooksPath .githooks` (or `cp .githooks/pre-commit .git/hooks/pre-commit`), placed with the other install commands at README.md:14-31; and (2) in the same change, make the count claims checkout-independent \u2014 either qualify them (\"in a checkout with hooks installed\") or replace them with a command+date form \u2014 and file the CI-005 self-sufficiency fix (read the