 {"id": "CLN-002", "type": "chore", "priority": "P3", "status": "pending", "title": "Repo hygiene: delete dead generate_index.py.handwritten — tracked, unreferenced copy walks .tmp (3942 junk entries) and takes 8.71s vs canonical 0.39s", "acceptance_criteria": "From /home/kara/speclang: (1) git ls-files generate_index.py.handwritten prints nothing and the file is absent from the working tree (git rm). (2) grep -rn generate_index.py.handwritten --include='*.py' --include='*.md' --include='*.sh' . prints no caller (exclude .git). (3) python3 scripts/generate_index.py --generate exits 0 and the regenerated _index.json contains no spec whose file value is under .tmp/ — jq '.specs | to_entries | map(select(.value.file | startswith(\".tmp/\"))) | length' prints 0. Restore _index.json afterward (git checkout -- _index.json) so the regenerated timestamp does not dirty the tree.", "reasoning": "MEASUREMENT (2026-11-18, SpecLang-perf tick SpecLang-perf-2026-11-18-13-57-02, measured HEAD 0bfc57b7). generate_index.py.handwritten (repo root, tracked since f62b7c33, zero callers — grep across *.py/*.md/*.sh finds no reference) is a dead superseded copy of the index generator. It walks the whole tree with os.walk and no excluded-dir guard (generate_index.py.handwritten:98-125), so it picks up the test suite's .tmp scratch: \"Found 4425 spec files\" of which 3942 live in .tmp and only ~476 in specs/. It then reads every file TWICE (line count at :142-143, then parse_header f.readlines() at :10-11). Measured wall 8.71s (2.15s user / 1.10s sys) at loadavg ~7-15 on 16 cores, producing a polluted _index.json of 4425 entries. The canonical scripts/generate_index.py --generate already carries EXCLUDED_DIRS = {.git,.opencode,.backup_spec_files,.tmp,_tmp,node_modules,.vfs,dist,coverage} (scripts/generate_index.py:190) and generates the correct index in 0.39s wall (0.31s user). FIX: delete generate_index.py.handwritten — dead code, superseded by the documented path (README:396-405). The canonical generator's own 4x-read (line-count + parse_header + extract_refs + extract_blocks) is NOT a finding: at ~481 files it is 0.39s, sub-second, not user-noticeable.", "capability_tags": ["hygiene"], "created_at": "2026-11-18T14:12:23Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-18T14:12:23Z", "depends_on": [], "detail": {"metadata": {}, "fingerprint": "45169c3a24f0d9d2ee3c3986c83611a9c995b4f3a31da29e755fe899c1015b1a"}, "complexity": 1}
 {"id": "DOC-10", "type": null, "priority": "P4", "status": "pending", "title": "P4 — HTTP route enumerations omit the shipped GET /metrics scrape endpoint (API_REFERENCE + GETTING-STARTED)", "acceptance_criteria": "From a clone of dexdat/SpecLang at origin/main (audit tree HEAD 1a2134ac), docs-only change, no code:\n1) `grep -c 'GET /metrics' docs/API_REFERENCE.md` prints >= 1, and the match sits inside the MCP HTTP route enumeration, not in an unrelated section: `git show HEAD:specs/docs.spec.dir/docs/API_REFERENCE.md | sed -n '180,210p'` shows `GET /metrics` listed alongside `GET /mcp`, `POST /mcp/message`, `GET /events`, `GET /health` (the writer may add one clause to the HTTP+SSE row and/or one bullet to the \"Transports actually implemented\" list).\n2) `grep -n '/metrics' GETTING-STARTED.md` prints a match on a row of the `--remote` route table that currently occupies lines 90-96 (`| \\`GET /metrics\\` | ... |`), so the table no longer stops at three routes.\n3) The added text states what the endpoint is and where the detail lives: the row/clause names Prometheus/OpenMetrics exposition and cites docs/observability-spec.md §9.1 (single source of truth for the family list — do not copy the family table into either page).\n4) Dual-view preserved: `readlink -f docs/API_REFERENCE.md` still resolves to specs/docs.spec.dir/docs/API_REFERENCE.md, and `git status --short` shows the SPEC TWIN path modified (docs/API_REFERENCE.md unchanged as a symlink). GETTING-STARTED.md is edited directly.\n5) Nothing else moves: `git diff --stat` touches exactly docs/API_REFERENCE.md (symlink) + specs/docs.spec.dir/docs/API_REFERENCE.md (twin) + GETTING-STARTED.md; `grep -c 'GET /metrics' docs/observability-spec.md` is unchanged (that file is already correct — do not edit it), and AGENTS.md is untouched.\n6) No code change: `node bin/speclang --help` still exits 0 and `git diff --stat -- src bin specs/mcp.spec.dir` is empty.\nVerifiable upstream fact the reviewer can re-run: `curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' http://127.0.0.1:<port>/metrics` against `node bin/speclang mcp start --remote --port <port>` returns 200 (this tick measured 200, Content-Type text/plain; version=0.0.4; charset=utf-8, 231 lines on fresh state).", "reasoning": "Doc severity is P4 by policy (docs-lane ruling: a shipped surface that the maintained reference cannot reach), not a functional-severity assessment. Precedent: DOC-7 (five shipped CLI commands missing from the same reference table) was filed and closed at P4. This row is NOT a re-file of DOC-1 (MCP tool inventory), DOC-7 (CLI verbs), DOC-8 (docs/layers.md links) or OBS-1 (which built the endpoint); those are complete and own different surfaces.\n\nWHAT IS WRONG. Two maintained pages enumerate the MCP HTTP route surface and both present the list as the complete set, but neither names GET /metrics — which the shipped binary serves:\n\n1. docs/API_REFERENCE.md:185 (the \"HTTP + SSE\" row of the transport table): \"`GET /mcp` opens the SSE stream, `POST /mcp/message` carries JSON-RPC, `GET /events` is the event feed (enabled unless `MCP_SSE_ENABLED=false`), `GET /health` returns `{\\\"status\\\":\\\"ok\\\",\\\"mode\\\":\\\"http\\\"}`\" — four routes, no `/metrics`.\n2. docs/API_REFERENCE.md:197-200 (\"Transports actually implemented (`src/mcp/server.ts`): exactly two.\") re-enumerates the same four routes and stops at `GET /health` (`server.ts:215`), never reaching `app.get('/metrics', …)` at `server.ts:225`.\n3. GETTING-STARTED.md:90-96: \"In `--remote` mode the server listens on:\" followed by a 3-row table (`GET /mcp`, `POST /mcp/message`, `GET /health`) — `/metrics` and `/events` are both absent.\n\nMEASURED AT origin/main. `git show origin/main:specs/mcp.spec.dir/src/server.ts | grep -n \\\"app\\\\.\\\\(get\\\\|post\\\\)('/\\\"` returns exactly five registrations: `/mcp` (94), `/mcp/message` (108), `/events` (205), `/health` (216), `/metrics` (225). `src/mcp/server.ts` is a symlink (git mode 120000) to that spec twin, so both paths name the same file — edit the spec side. The endpoint itself landed 2026-11-17 in 7adc5dcf \"feat: add Prometheus /metrics scrape endpoint exposing speclang_ series. Addresses OBS-1.\" and is already documented in docs/observability-spec.md §9.1 (with Content-Type, registry module and test file) — so the detail doc exists; the two route enumerations simply were never updated.\n\nLIVE PROBE (run this tick, scratch state, non-default port 19881, scratch dir /mnt/ssd/tmp/speclang-obs-probe.ZoXV9w):\n  $ node bin/speclang mcp start --remote --port 19877 -d <scratch>\n  SpecLang MCP server running on http://localhost:19877\n    MCP endpoint: http://localhost:19877/mcp\n    Events endpoint: http://localhost:19877/events\n    Metrics endpoint: http://localhost:19877/metrics\n  $ curl -s -D - -o metrics.txt http://127.0.0.1:19881/metrics\n  HTTP/1.1 200 OK\n  Content-Type: text/plain; version=0.0.4; charset=utf-8\n  (231 lines, 4 `speclang_pipeline_*` families declared with HELP/TYPE and zero series on fresh state)\nThe server's own startup banner advertises the Metrics endpoint that neither maintained page lists — a reader of the reference cannot discover the scrape surface, and a monitoring integrator reading API_REFERENCE concludes the surface is four routes.\n\nFIX DIRECTION (writer's choice on wording, not on coverage). Add `GET /metrics` to the transport row at docs/API_REFERENCE.md:185 AND to the enumeration at :200-204 (one clause is enough: Prometheus/OpenMetrics exposition, `text/plain; version=0.0.4; charset=utf-8`, no auth — middleware is mounted on `/mcp` only, see :204), and add a `GET /metrics` row to the `--remote` table at GETTING-STARTED.md:90-96. Point at docs/observability-spec.md §9.1 as the authoritative detail rather than duplicating the family list. `/events` is already named in API_REFERENCE:185/:200 — only GETTING-STARTED's table omits it; adding that row too is in scope but secondary to `/metrics`.\n\nDUAL-VIEW TRAP. docs/API_REFERENCE.md is a symlink to ../specs/docs.spec.dir/docs/API_REFERENCE.md (resolves today); the edit must land on the spec twin, so the worker will see the specs/ path modified in `git status` and the symlink itself unchanged — that is correct, do not \"fix\" the symlink. GETTING-STARTED.md is a plain tracked file (not a symlink). Do not touch docs/observability-spec.md, which is already correct, and do not edit AGENTS.md.\n\nAUDIENCE: integrator/operator wiring a scrape (Prometheus, fleet monitoring) and any developer reading the reference. ARTIFACT: docs/API_REFERENCE.md (spec twin specs/docs.spec.dir/docs/API_REFERENCE.md) + GETTING-STARTED.md.\n\nEVIDENCE ARTIFACT: /home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/docs/speclang/audit-2026-11-18-13-57-02.md (probe scripts probe-mcp-2026-11-18.sh, probe-obs-2026-11-18.sh in the same directory; raw ordering in the report's probe section). Measured at HEAD 1a2134ac (origin/main tip at audit time), 2026-11-18.\n\nch:trace row=DOC-10 spec=docs/API_REFERENCE.md#3-mcp-server wave=none:serial-audit test=none:open-finding doc=docs/API_REFERENCE.md,GETTING-STARTED.md prompt=/home/kara/.hermes/skills/docs-gap-audit-lane/SKILL.md evidence=/home/kara/.hermes/stand-in/docs/speclang/audit-2026-11-18-13-57-02.md witness=live:http://127.0.0.1:19881/metrics verdict=none:open-finding commit=none:open memory=none:exact-key-not-found", "capability_tags": ["docs"], "created_at": "2026-11-18T14:25:49Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-18T14:25:49Z", "depends_on": [], "detail": {"fingerprint": "66e72554bd54333f1cfca618847d17f98a7944cec67105d300b93e52479de0ff"}, "complexity": 3}
